senses.gloss:
dupadendra (MIndic for Skt. dvi˚; cf. du-; dupada not recorded in Pali; AMg. dupaya acc. to Sheth),
(1) king: in Gv 〔259.20〕 (vs) read, yada sa niṣkramī dupadendrā (or ˚dro), when that king retired from the world;
(2) n. of a former Buddha: in Gv 〔258.8〕 (vs) read with 2d ed., saptamu teṣa āsi Dupadendraḥ.
